WHAT: WK_TFE_SELFTEST=1 makes the app narrate itself on stdout -- platform,
      style, font count, screen size, then a repeating STATE line (window
      title, torrent name, info hash, total size, file-list row count, number
      of visible top-levels) and a BTNABOUT line with the About button's rect
      in surface coordinates.
WHY:  TEST SCAFFOLDING, and the only kind that catches the failures that
      matter here. A headless harness can read pixels, but a pixel histogram
      proves "not blank" -- it cannot tell a rendered torrent from a rendered
      empty form. These lines come out of BencodeModel, so they prove the
      .torrent arriving over a wk BindMount was actually PARSED. The published
      rect is what lets the harness aim a genuine wasi:surface pointer event
      at a real button and watch a second top-level window appear, which is
      the whole input path plus multi-window compositing.
      Rect published on a repeating timer, not once: the wk QPA forces the
      first top-level to the full surface, so any rect read at singleShot(0)
      predates that resize and aiming at it misses. The repeat doubles as the
      only evidence that QTimer deadlines survive being folded into the frame
      wait.
UPSTREAM: no. This is ours, for testing, and it is #ifdef __wasi__ so it does
      not exist in a desktop build. Upstream would rightly want this as a
      QTest, which cannot run here (FEATURE_testlib=OFF, and a wasip2
      component has no test harness).
